00:27:53,533 --> 00:27:55,803
The pieces come together perfectly.

773
00:27:55,963 --> 00:27:59,373
I think that's pretty fun.

774
00:28:01,373 --> 00:28:03,672
(To be continued)

775
00:28:03,673 --> 00:28:06,273
- Between the rocks... - What's this?

776
00:28:06,813 --> 00:28:07,813
My heart is fluttering.

777
00:28:08,383 --> 00:28:10,113
(Servant84 is working hard to restore the stone wall.)

778
00:28:11,483 --> 00:28:13,983
- Between the rocks... - What's this?

779
00:28:15,493 --> 00:28:16,693
Like this, fill up the space between the rocks.

780
00:28:16,953 --> 00:28:18,863
- My heart is fluttering. - It's like a music video.

781
00:28:20,963 --> 00:28:21,963
So that they fit...

782
00:28:21,964 --> 00:28:23,532
(He fills up the empty spots with his diligence.)

783
00:28:23,533 --> 00:28:25,263
- There. - It's the shot of your first love.

784
00:28:27,473 --> 00:28:31,873
(Boyfriend at the library)

785
00:28:32,543 --> 00:28:33,702
He looks the same.

786
00:28:33,703 --> 00:28:35,273
(Boyfriend at the tangerine field)

787
00:28:35,443 --> 00:28:36,842
- First love. - It's like an ad of Jeju water.

788
00:28:36,843 --> 00:28:38,513
(It's like a commercial.)

789
00:28:41,813 --> 00:28:42,852
Kian84.

790
00:28:42,853 --> 00:28:44,123
(The senior we loved back then, Hee Min)

791
00:28:44,883 --> 00:28:45,883
There.

792
00:28:47,693 --> 00:28:48,693
It's cool.

793
00:28:50,323 --> 00:28:51,622
(He stays cool until the end when he restores the stone wall.)

794
00:28:51,623 --> 00:28:52,623
There.

795
00:28:53,593 --> 00:28:55,932
Now, the stone wall won't collapse no matter what.

796
00:28:55,933 --> 00:28:56,963
- Okay. - Follow me.

797
00:28:57,503 --> 00:28:59,902
- Let's go to the auntie's side. - There is so much work.

798
00:28:59,903 --> 00:29:01,273
- There are rocks, right? - Yes.

799
00:29:01,903 --> 00:29:04,972
Pick up the rocks.

800
00:29:04,973 --> 00:29:07,642
(Pick up the rocks on the ground and put them on the side.)

801
00:29:07,643 --> 00:29:11,782
- Pile up the rocks on the side. - Okay.

802
00:29:11,783 --> 00:29:12,783
Shall I pile them up?

803
00:29:12,784 --> 00:29:15,913
We need to move the rocks we've collected.

804
00:29:16,083 --> 00:29:18,023
- Okay. - In Jeju dialect, it's "Eoyeom."

805
00:29:18,453 --> 00:29:19,583
- "Eoyeom?" - Yes.

806
00:29:19,883 --> 00:29:21,193
- "Eoyeom?" - What's that?

807
00:29:21,323 --> 00:29:22,592
It means "Side."

808
00:29:22,593 --> 00:29:24,023
- Side. - Yes.

809
00:29:24,493 --> 00:29:26,323
- "Eoyeop?" - Eoyeom.

810
00:29:26,463 --> 00:29:27,862
- Eoyeom. - Eoyeom.

811
00:29:27,863 --> 00:29:29,892
- Side. - Yes. Side.

812
00:29:29,893 --> 00:29:31,033
("Eoyeom" means "Side," right?)

813
00:29:31,333 --> 00:29:33,063
Are you from Jeju Island?

814
00:29:33,263 --> 00:29:34,832
- I'm a native. - Are you a native?

815
00:29:34,833 --> 00:29:35,833
I see.

816
00:29:36,003 --> 00:29:38,273
You won't understand me if I use the Jeju dialect.

817
00:29:38,403 --> 00:29:40,702
Would you say something?

818
00:29:40,703 --> 00:29:41,713
(He becomes curious.)

819
00:29:42,343 --> 00:29:44,813
Gosh, you sokakjeoing to come here.

820
00:29:45,143 --> 00:29:46,713
"You sokakjeoing to come here."

821
00:29:47,513 --> 00:29:49,783
"You must've gotten fooled to come here."

822
00:29:50,053 --> 00:29:51,223
Does it mean something else?

823
00:29:51,523 --> 00:29:52,722
It means that you've struggled.

824
00:29:52,723 --> 00:29:54,252
- Is that the meaning? - Yes.

825
00:29:54,253 --> 00:29:55,293
(It means that he has struggled.)

826
00:29:55,453 --> 00:29:56,722
"When Life Gives You Tangerines..."

827
00:29:56,723 --> 00:29:58,023
- has taught us that. - Yes.

828
00:29:59,493 --> 00:30:02,262
Do you know what this is called in Jeju dialect?

829
00:30:02,263 --> 00:30:03,332
What?

830
00:30:03,333 --> 00:30:05,003
What is this called in Jeju dialect?

831
00:30:05,063 --> 00:30:06,163
Sickle?

832
00:30:06,333 --> 00:30:07,733
- Homi. - "Homi?"

833
00:30:07,873 --> 00:30:09,332
- What? - Really?

834
00:30:09,333 --> 00:30:12,503
What we call "Homi" is a triangular tool.

835
00:30:13,503 --> 00:30:14,743
That's gwolgaengi.

836
00:30:15,013 --> 00:30:16,372
- "Gwolgaengi?" - Gwolgaengi.

837
00:30:16,373 --> 00:30:18,313
- What's that called? - Homi.

838
00:30:18,743 --> 00:30:20,113
People call it "Homi" in Seoul too.

839
00:30:20,313 --> 00:30:21,412
We call it a sickle.

840
00:30:21,413 --> 00:30:23,013
- Really? - No, we call it a sickle.

841
00:30:23,713 --> 00:30:24,923
- Sickle. - Homi.

842
00:30:25,253 --> 00:30:26,722
- Is a sickle called "Homi?" - Yes.

843
00:30:26,723 --> 00:30:28,592
(He finally understands.)

844
00:30:28,593 --> 00:30:29,722
It's different.

845
00:30:29,723 --> 00:30:31,622
What you call "Homi" in Seoul is called "Gwolgaengi" here.

846
00:30:31,623 --> 00:30:32,762
Here, this is "Homi."

847
00:30:32,763 --> 00:30:34,233
- Is that "Homi?" - Yes.

848
00:30:34,693 --> 00:30:35,732
It's different.

849
00:30:35,733 --> 00:30:37,533
Brother, give me the sickle!

850
00:30:39,963 --> 00:30:44,033
(Brother, give me the sickle!)

851
00:30:44,243 --> 00:30:45,402
(You said that a sickle was called "Homi" on Jeju Island.)

852
00:30:45,403 --> 00:30:46,643
What?

853
00:30:47,913 --> 00:30:49,813
It's so funny to see him walk away without a word.

854
00:30:50,673 --> 00:30:52,113
He asked for the sickle, and he understood that.

855
00:30:54,143 --> 00:30:56,653
(He is funny.)

856
00:30:59,723 --> 00:31:01,293
(Let's hurry up and move the rocks.)

857
00:31:02,453 --> 00:31:03,852
Fields on Jeju Island are...

858
00:31:03,853 --> 00:31:06,192
- half soil and half rocks. - Right.

859
00:31:06,193 --> 00:31:07,563
It'll take me forever to move the rocks.

860
00:31:09,533 --> 00:31:10,592
(Grunting)

861
00:31:10,593 --> 00:31:11,963
Gosh, these rocks.

862
00:31:12,933 --> 00:31:14,473
Gosh, look at all these rocks.

863
00:31:24,513 --> 00:31:26,212
(Meanwhile, his fur siblings are receiving education.)

864
00:31:26,213 --> 00:31:27,382
Alkong.

865
00:31:27,383 --> 00:31:28,513
(Meanwhile, his fur siblings are receiving education.)

866
00:31:28,653 --> 00:31:29,753
Let's go.

867
00:31:31,723 --> 00:31:33,082
A person does manual labor...

868
00:31:33,083 --> 00:31:34,223
while dogs receive education.

869
00:31:39,663 --> 00:31:41,733
(He spreads fertilizer.)

870
00:31:43,133 --> 00:31:46,133
