00:37:47,093 --> 00:37:49,032
The real son is struggling a lot.

1036
00:37:49,033 --> 00:37:50,733
(His nose becomes very runny.)

1037
00:37:51,333 --> 00:37:53,003
Please look over here.

1038
00:37:54,003 --> 00:37:55,003
(Sneezing)

1039
00:37:56,433 --> 00:37:57,602
(He can't help but sneeze.)

1040
00:37:57,603 --> 00:37:58,772
All right.

1041
00:37:58,773 --> 00:37:59,902
That's...

1042
00:37:59,903 --> 00:38:02,273
(1 second before sneezing)

1043
00:38:04,013 --> 00:38:05,113
That's a good one.

1044
00:38:05,613 --> 00:38:07,083
They take amazing photos.

1045
00:38:07,883 --> 00:38:09,852
- I'm sorry. - You're struggling a lot.

1046
00:38:09,853 --> 00:38:11,212
- Shall I hold them? - Yes.

1047
00:38:11,213 --> 00:38:12,952
Where is your mom?

1048
00:38:12,953 --> 00:38:14,583
- Dalkong, stay. - Where is your mom?

1049
00:38:15,053 --> 00:38:16,822
Mom.

1050
00:38:16,823 --> 00:38:19,193
Mom.

1051
00:38:19,393 --> 00:38:20,462
- Mom. - You look beautiful, Mom.

1052
00:38:20,463 --> 00:38:21,563
Please arrange your hair.

1053
00:38:22,463 --> 00:38:23,463
Alkong, look at Mom.

1054
00:38:23,464 --> 00:38:26,003
I wouldn't call myself a filial son.

1055
00:38:26,733 --> 00:38:28,302
There are many sons like me.

1056
00:38:28,303 --> 00:38:29,403
That isn't true.

1057
00:38:30,333 --> 00:38:31,643
I think they're about the same.

1058
00:38:32,543 --> 00:38:35,773
After Candy passed away,

1059
00:38:36,313 --> 00:38:39,643
the atmosphere was very depressed and quiet at home.

1060
00:38:40,883 --> 00:38:45,253
Those dogs bring energy into the house.

1061
00:38:45,883 --> 00:38:46,983
I'm thankful for them.

1062
00:38:47,553 --> 00:38:48,953
- Those are amazing photos. - How cute.

1063
00:38:49,853 --> 00:38:51,223
Mom said this.

1064
00:38:51,763 --> 00:38:55,693
"Hee Min, don't think that you're a good person..."

1065
00:38:56,263 --> 00:38:57,493
"for bringing stray dogs."

1066
00:38:58,103 --> 00:39:01,262
"We became happy..."

1067
00:39:01,263 --> 00:39:03,703
"because they chose us."

1068
00:39:04,373 --> 00:39:05,573
To be honest,

1069
00:39:05,773 --> 00:39:07,443
I thought it was my good deed.

1070
00:39:07,903 --> 00:39:09,843
- It's true. - I thought it was my good deed.

1071
00:39:11,073 --> 00:39:12,543
(Well...)

1072
00:39:12,883 --> 00:39:15,983
In any case, I think...

1073
00:39:17,183 --> 00:39:20,683
it's a win-win situation for us and the dogs.

1074
00:39:21,523 --> 00:39:23,422
Let's go.

1075
00:39:23,423 --> 00:39:25,292
- Well done. - Thank you.

1076
00:39:25,293 --> 00:39:27,322
- Thank you for your hard work. - Thank you.

1077
00:39:27,323 --> 00:39:29,993
- Thank you. Take care. - Alkong and Dalkong, stay healthy.

1078
00:39:30,393 --> 00:39:32,063
He wants Mom to hold him.

1079
00:39:32,203 --> 00:39:33,902
He loves Mom so much.

1080
00:39:33,903 --> 00:39:35,732
Let's go and get some medicine.

1081
00:39:35,733 --> 00:39:36,802
You need medicine.

1082
00:39:36,803 --> 00:39:38,703
We can go to the pharmacy.

1083
00:39:40,473 --> 00:39:42,812
- Let's hurry. - Mom! This way.

1084
00:39:42,813 --> 00:39:44,512
There's one over there.

1085
00:39:44,513 --> 00:39:46,812
(The Reliable Furry Siblings Next to the Awkward Good Son)

1086
00:39:46,813 --> 00:39:47,842
(I Live Alone)

1087
00:39:47,843 --> 00:39:49,882
- It's great to see you! - It's great to see you!

1088
00:39:49,883 --> 00:39:51,922
There's great news for our Rainbow Club.

1089
00:39:51,923 --> 00:39:54,422
At the Baeksang Arts Awards,

1090
00:39:54,423 --> 00:39:56,022
Kian84 won the Male Entertainer Award!

1091
00:39:56,023 --> 00:39:57,493
- Yes! - Yes!

1092
00:39:57,553 --> 00:39:59,393
Congratulations!

1093
00:39:59,523 --> 00:40:01,393
It was a vivid moment.

1094
00:40:02,593 --> 00:40:04,692
When he went up to receive the reward,

1095
00:40:04,693 --> 00:40:05,963
I felt emotional.

1096
00:40:06,163 --> 00:40:07,462
- Really? - I'm so happy for you.

1097
00:40:07,463 --> 00:40:09,133
- I watched it live. - Thank you.

1098
00:40:09,303 --> 00:40:11,102
I've learned so much from you.

1099
00:40:11,103 --> 00:40:13,402
- Thank you so much. - Congratulations once again.

1100
00:40:13,403 --> 00:40:14,842
Kian84 has...

1101
00:40:14,843 --> 00:40:16,643
written history in the variety show world.

1102
00:40:16,743 --> 00:40:18,313
- Right. - Right.

1103
00:40:18,513 --> 00:40:20,042
Just like Kian84 who has just received an award,

1104
00:40:20,043 --> 00:40:22,952
this person is really popular in variety shows these days.

1105
00:40:22,953 --> 00:40:25,653
The preview of him got so many views.

1106
00:40:25,853 --> 00:40:27,652
Please welcome Lee Seon Min!

1107
00:40:27,653 --> 00:40:30,023
(Lee Seon Min)

1108
00:40:30,853 --> 00:40:32,623
(What did your wife say?)

1109
00:40:32,723 --> 00:40:33,923
(I'm single.)

1110
00:40:34,563 --> 00:40:35,633
(The one who certainly looks like a married man)

1111
00:40:35,833 --> 00:40:38,363
(Views: 1.83 million, 1.59 million, and 1.22 million)

1112
00:40:38,903 --> 00:40:40,933
(He took over YouTube with his energy.)

1113
00:40:41,773 --> 00:40:43,202
(The comedian with 10 years of experience...)

1114
00:40:43,203 --> 00:40:44,633
(who is showing a great performance everywhere)

1115
00:40:45,903 --> 00:40:48,143
Right. Hello, everyone.

1116
00:40:48,243 --> 00:40:51,072
I've been living alone for 19 years.

1117
00:40:51,073 --> 00:40:52,743
I'm Comedian Lee Seon Min. Hello!

1118
00:40:55,013 --> 00:40:56,583
You're not older than me, right?

1119
00:40:56,953 --> 00:40:58,053
I was born in the Year of the Dragon.

1120
00:40:58,623 --> 00:41:00,323
- So that's 1976? - No.

1121
00:41:01,253 --> 00:41:02,993
- You were born in 1988? - Right.

1122
00:41:03,093 --> 00:41:04,423
I was born in 1988.

1123
00:41:04,923 --> 00:41:06,662
I'm the same age as G-DRAGON.

1124
00:41:06,663 --> 00:41:08,092
- G-DRAGON? - Right.

1125
00:41:08,093 --> 00:41:09,093
Right.

1126
00:41:09,094 --> 00:41:11,233
- It's my first time meeting him. - Right.

1127
00:41:11,463 --> 00:41:12,832
- But his eyes... - Right.

1128
00:41:12,833 --> 00:41:14,532
- The color of his eyes... - He looks like a foreigner.

1129
00:41:14,533 --> 00:41:15,802
- The color of his eyes is unique. - Right.

1130
00:41:15,803 --> 00:41:17,272
I have olive eyes.

1131
00:41:17,273 --> 00:41:19,043
- Right. - I've never seen that color before.

1132
00:41:19,403 --> 00:41:21,273
There's someone else who has similar eyes as me.

1133
00:41:21,773 --> 00:41:24,173
- Seo Kang Jun. - I see.

1134
00:41:24,783 --> 00:41:27,182
- Just the eyes are similar. - Right.

1135
00:41:27,183 --> 00:41:28,313
There's Go A Ra as well.

1136
00:41:29,153 --> 00:41:30,612
- Lee Sung Kyoung. - Just the eyes.

1137
00:41:30,613 --> 00:41:32,753
- Just the color of the eyes. - Right.

1138
00:41:33,123 --> 00:41:34,123
(Laughing)

1139
00:41:34,124 --> 00:41:36,092
He has lived alone for 19 years.

1140
00:41:36,093 --> 00:41:37,752
He's truly single. He has never gotten married.

1141
00:41:37,753 --> 00:41:38,892
- That's right. - Truly single?

1142
00:41:38,893 --> 00:41:40,093
He's truly single.

1143
00:41:40,723 --> 00:41:42,733
Let's dive into Lee Seon Min's life!

1144
00:41:45,203 --> 00:41:48,133
(The Single Man of Certainty)

1145
00:41:49,103 --> 00:41:52,673
(The room is dark because of the blackout curtains.)

1146
00:41:59,613 --> 00:42:00,682
- What is that? - What is that?

1147
00:42:00,683 --> 00:42:01,713
Isn't that a respirator?

1148
00:42:02,453 --> 00:42:03,453
That's a PAP machine.

1149
00:42:03,454 --> 00:42:06,483
People who have bad snoring or sleep apnea issues use that.

1150
00:42:06,953 --> 00:42:08,952
It continuously applies air pressure into the nose.

1151
00:42:08,953 --> 00:42:09,953
Right.

1152
00:42:10,593 --> 00:42:14,123
(He's sleeping with the PAP machine on.)

1153
00:42:16,233 --> 00:42:17,863
He looks like a man from the future.

1154
00:42:20,163 --> 00:42:21,233
Hello.

1155
00:42:21,603 --> 00:42:24,633
I've lived alone for 19 years. I'm Comedian Lee Seon Min.

1156
00:42:25,173 --> 00:42:27,373
It feels like he was married once.

1157
00:42:28,613 --> 00:42:29,643
That's what it feels like.

1158
00:42:33,343 --> 00:42:34,883
He's wearing such cute pajamas.

1159
00:42:37,183 --> 00:42:38,723
- He looks like a baby. - Right.

1160
00:42:39,053 --> 00:42:40,183
A very big baby.

1161
00:42:41,023 --> 00:42:42,623
(Crying)

1162
00:42:46,293 --> 00:42:49,033
(He does a stretch.)

1163
00:42:50,863 --> 00:42:53,463
(Getting up)

1164
00:43:06,313 --> 00:43:08,813
If I remember it correctly, I moved places ten times.

1165
00:43:09,313 --> 00:43:11,583
I believe this is my 11th house.

1166
00:43:11,653 --> 00:43:14,753
I moved to Seoul when I was 21.

1167
00:43:14,823 --> 00:43:16,523
I started living in a boarding house.

1168
00:43:16,653 --> 00:43:19,263
I've lived in a gosiwon and a studio apartment.

1169
00:43:19,493 --> 00:43:23,893
I've also lived in a rooftop house and a semi-basement house.

1170
00:43:24,533 --> 00:43:27,663
I've made it here after living in those places.

1171
00:43:28,473 --> 00:43:30,773
And as I've lived alone for 19 years,

1172
00:43:31,133 --> 00:43:33,903
I brought with me all of my belongings.

1173
00:43:34,143 --> 00:43:37,473
They're stuck in each corner of the house.

1174
00:43:37,643 --> 00:43:39,982
Right. You keep getting more things as you live alone.

1175
00:43:39,983 --> 00:43:41,142
- Right. - You keep getting more things.

1176
00:43:41,143 --> 00:43:42,183
Unnecessary things should be thrown out.

1177
00:43:42,683 --> 00:43:45,083
(In the middle of the spacious living room,)

1178
00:43:45,853 --> 00:43:49,593
(there are 2 large drying racks!)

1179
00:43:53,593 --> 00:43:54,663
The Christmas tree is still up.

1180
00:43:55,293 --> 00:43:56,493
Shouldn't this be thrown out?

1181
00:43:57,733 --> 00:44:00,333
That tree to me...

1182
00:44:00,803 --> 00:44:02,273
is like a veteran tree.

1183
00:44:02,803 --> 00:44:03,972
- A veteran tree? - Right.

1184
00:44:03,973 --> 00:44:05,742
- A veteran tree at home? - That tree feels like...

1185
00:44:05,743 --> 00:44:07,902
- it will protect me. - I see.

1186
00:44:07,903 --> 00:44:09,713
It brings a sense of comfort.

1187
00:44:10,713 --> 00:44:13,483
(Next to the living room with the veteran tree,)

1188
00:44:15,053 --> 00:44:17,753
(there's a kitchen with a lot of traces of life.)

1189
00:44:18,553 --> 00:44:20,052
There are a lot of things.

1190
00:44:20,053 --> 00:44:21,992
Right. They're still in place.

1191
00:44:21,993 --> 00:44:22,993
(There are many supplements that kept him healthy for 19 years.)

1192
00:44:23,323 --> 00:44:24,722
(The dressing room...)

1193
00:44:24,723 --> 00:44:27,123
(is filled with clothes beyond its limit.)

1194
00:44:28,023 --> 00:44:29,762
(There are many clothes in the bedroom as well.)

1195
00:44:29,763 --> 00:44:30,962
Why are there so many clothes?

1196
00:44:30,963 --> 00:44:32,133
It's just like my house.

1197
00:44:32,763 --> 00:44:34,903
- We're all the same. - We're all the same.

1198
00:44:37,303 --> 00:44:39,543
(Scratching)

1199
00:44:40,303 --> 00:44:41,342
(Rubbing)

1200
00:44:41,343 --> 00:44:42,473
(Sniffling)

1201
00:44:44,113 --> 00:44:47,583
(Gosh, I should get up.)

1202
00:44:48,913 --> 00:44:52,853
(He heads over to the kitchen after barely managing to get up.)

1203
00:45:01,733 --> 00:45:04,263
(Scratching)

1204
00:45:09,103 --> 00:45:12,243
(He drinks a cup of water on an empty stomach.)

1205
00:45:13,573 --> 00:45:17,613
(He opens the fridge after quenching his thirst.)

1206
00:45:21,143 --> 00:45:22,152
(The fridge is packed.)

1207
00:45:22,153 --> 00:45:24,553
- It's well-organized. - It looks well-organized.

1208
00:45:25,683 --> 00:45:29,053
(Thinking)

1209
00:45:30,193 --> 00:45:33,193
(He grabs something after thinking for a while.)

1210
00:45:33,823 --> 00:45:35,663
(Tossing)

1211
00:45:36,463 --> 00:45:37,732
(Did he take out leftover ingredients from the fridge?)

1212
00:45:37,733 --> 00:45:39,563
- He must be cooking. - He must be cooking.

1213
00:45:41,103 --> 00:45:43,273
(Taking out)

1214
00:45:44,173 --> 00:45:45,902
(He gets out the leftover meat as well.)

1215
00:45:45,903 --> 00:45:49,513
I don't throw out any of the ingredients I have.

1216
00:45:49,613 --> 00:45:51,883
- I see. You use them later. - Right.

1217
00:45:55,013 --> 00:45:57,452
(He checks the doenjang by smelling it.)

1218
00:45:57,453 --> 00:45:59,752
- You check by the smell. - Right.

1219
00:45:59,753 --> 00:46:02,023
I believe that pastes...

1220
00:46:02,453 --> 00:46:04,493
can be kept for a long time.

1221
00:46:04,723 --> 00:46:06,493
So I don't throw them out.

1222
00:46:06,993 --> 00:46:09,233
(After getting out the ingredients,)

1223
00:46:11,063 --> 00:46:12,162
(he grabs the rice bag.)

1224
00:46:12,163 --> 00:46:13,163
He's making rice.

1225
00:46:14,603 --> 00:46:18,403
(He measures it by eye.)

1226
00:46:19,043 --> 00:46:20,472
Gosh, he's making rice?

1227
00:46:20,473 --> 00:46:21,972
I make rice as well these days.

1228
00:46:21,973 --> 00:46:23,113
- Really? - Yes.

1229
00:46:23,143 --> 00:46:24,173
Isn't it too much work?

1230
00:46:24,713 --> 00:46:27,343
But doing that on my day off...

1231
00:46:27,743 --> 00:46:29,452
- gives me peace. - It must make you happy.

1232
00:46:29,453 --> 00:46:30,512
Making rice is a pleasant thing to do.

1233
00:46:30,513 --> 00:46:31,653
- It must be a hobby. - Right.

1234
00:46:33,153 --> 00:46:34,823
(Collecting)

1235
00:46:36,193 --> 00:46:38,123
(Dripping)

1236
00:46:39,763 --> 00:46:41,323
He just estimates it.

1237
00:46:41,463 --> 00:46:42,662
I always put my hand in...

1238
00:46:42,663 --> 00:46:44,533
- Same here. - and do what I learned to do.

1239
00:46:45,833 --> 00:46:49,173
(It will take 30 minutes to cook.)

1240
00:46:49,833 --> 00:46:53,473
(He grabs the frying pan and pot after preparing the rice.)

1241
00:46:56,543 --> 00:46:59,043
(He gets a good amount of water in the pot.)

1242
00:47:00,083 --> 00:47:01,543
(He throws in some kelp...)

1243
00:47:02,983 --> 00:47:05,153
(and frozen anchovies.)

1244
00:47:08,653 --> 00:47:11,323
- It's a broth. - You're making a broth?

1245
00:47:11,823 --> 00:47:14,493
I make a broth for any kind of jjigae.

1246
00:47:15,463 --> 00:47:18,862
Why don't you use the broth packs that are sold?

1247
00:47:18,863 --> 00:47:22,572
There are times when it contains ingredients I don't want.

1248
00:47:22,573 --> 00:47:23,702
- Right. - I see.

1249
00:47:23,703 --> 00:47:26,042
There are times when it contains dried shrimp.

1250
00:47:26,043 --> 00:47:29,372
Right. That is why I only use kelp and big anchovies.

1251
00:47:29,373 --> 00:47:32,142
- That's all that is needed. - I use just a lot of those.

1252
00:47:32,143 --> 00:47:35,413
The kelp and anchovies bought last for around two years.

1253
00:47:35,713 --> 00:47:36,952
- They last for a long time. - Broth packs can be used...

1254
00:47:36,953 --> 00:47:38,152
about ten times.

1255
00:47:38,153 --> 00:47:39,153
- Right. - Right.

1256
00:47:39,183 --> 00:47:40,882
There are some types of ramyeon that have kelp in them.

1257
00:47:40,883 --> 00:47:41,892
- Right. - Right.

1258
00:47:41,893 --> 00:47:44,452
I add ten more pieces of kelp when I have those.

1259
00:47:44,453 --> 00:47:45,593
You add more.

1260
00:47:45,823 --> 00:47:47,693
- You like kelp? - I do.

1261
00:47:48,563 --> 00:47:51,793
I got kelp candy as a gift. I should've brought it.

1262
00:47:52,063 --> 00:47:53,102
- Kelp candy? - Right.

1263
00:47:53,103 --> 00:47:54,402
You can have all of it.

1264
00:47:54,403 --> 00:47:58,402
(It's okay. You can have all of it.)

1265
00:47:58,403 --> 00:47:59,872
- I don't need the candy. - He's so polite.

1266
00:47:59,873 --> 00:48:01,173
It doesn't sound pleasant.

1267
00:48:02,773 --> 00:48:05,343
(He grabs the cabbage while the broth boils.)

1268
00:48:06,083 --> 00:48:08,243
(He washes just what he needs.)

1269
00:48:10,083 --> 00:48:11,353
They're big pieces.

1270
00:48:11,513 --> 00:48:12,982
That's a man who lives alone.

1271
00:48:12,983 --> 00:48:14,053
Right.

1272
00:48:14,723 --> 00:48:17,253
(He takes out another bowl.)

1273
00:48:22,463 --> 00:48:25,463
(He throws in the meat into the bowl.)

1274
00:48:26,003 --> 00:48:29,003
In my 20s, I ate twice as much as I eat now.

1275
00:48:29,233 --> 00:48:31,902
When I bought ingredients back then,

1276
00:48:31,903 --> 00:48:33,342
there were barely any leftovers.

1277
00:48:33,343 --> 00:48:36,773
But as I eat less often at home now,

1278
00:48:37,243 --> 00:48:39,583
I end up throwing out a lot of the ingredients.

1279
00:48:39,813 --> 00:48:41,482
Whenever there are leftover ingredients,

1280
00:48:41,483 --> 00:48:44,313
I try to make something with them.

1281
00:48:44,553 --> 00:48:47,723
I try my best not to throw out ingredients.

1282
00:48:48,993 --> 00:48:51,223
(Seon Min is cooking with leftover ingredients again.)

1283
00:48:51,853 --> 00:48:54,193
(He washes the garlic that was left in the fridge.)

1284
00:48:55,393 --> 00:48:58,603
(He slices the garlic skillfully.)

1285
00:49:01,303 --> 00:49:03,133
(Taking out)

1286
00:49:04,733 --> 00:49:06,243
- Gosh! - A mortar?

1287
00:49:06,503 --> 00:49:08,042
It's been a while to see a mortar.

1288
00:49:08,043 --> 00:49:09,673
I saw those when I was in elementary school.

1289
00:49:10,173 --> 00:49:11,512
(He crushes the garlic right away.)

1290
00:49:11,513 --> 00:49:13,183
