- What? - What? You're leaving like that?

1806
01:11:40,203 --> 01:11:42,533
(He quickly packed his stuff.)

1807
01:11:43,533 --> 01:11:44,703
- You got it! - Okay.

1808
01:11:45,903 --> 01:11:47,443
- What's with that old man? - Who's he?

1809
01:11:49,713 --> 01:11:51,172
That's brave of him, though.

1810
01:11:51,173 --> 01:11:52,573
- Seriously. - To do that at the mountain gym.

1811
01:11:52,813 --> 01:11:54,482
I was so proud of him.

1812
01:11:54,483 --> 01:11:55,943
I feel like he'd become someone, though.

1813
01:11:56,453 --> 01:11:59,553
(He goes somewhere without taking a break.)

1814
01:12:00,753 --> 01:12:04,153
(Fully enjoying the phytoncide in the mountain)

1815
01:12:05,023 --> 01:12:06,123
(Breathing out)

1816
01:12:07,293 --> 01:12:08,493
Gosh, this is nice.

1817
01:12:08,663 --> 01:12:11,132
Lying around at home is surely nice,

1818
01:12:11,133 --> 01:12:13,703
but when the sunlight is nice, I'd sleep an hour or two less...

1819
01:12:14,033 --> 01:12:15,333
even though it's tiring.

1820
01:12:15,703 --> 01:12:18,973
I must go out and get moving while getting the sunlight...

1821
01:12:19,603 --> 01:12:21,803
to recharge my energy.

1822
01:12:22,103 --> 01:12:26,643
I think that's my driving force.

1823
01:12:26,983 --> 01:12:28,483
That's how I'm like too.

1824
01:12:29,513 --> 01:12:33,223
(Climbing down the mountain after recharging)

1825
01:12:34,253 --> 01:12:35,622
You feel rather better...

1826
01:12:35,623 --> 01:12:36,853
- if you go out. - That's true.

1827
01:12:37,923 --> 01:12:39,592
(After hiking, he diligently heads somewhere.)

1828
01:12:39,593 --> 01:12:41,463
- He's not going home. - He's going somewhere.

1829
01:12:46,233 --> 01:12:47,303
My gosh!

1830
01:12:48,398 --> 01:12:50,668
(After hiking, he diligently heads somewhere.)

1831
01:12:54,838 --> 01:12:55,948
My gosh!

1832
01:12:56,708 --> 01:12:57,847
(Clunk)

1833
01:12:57,848 --> 01:12:59,118
- Wait! Timeout! - Oh, my.

1834
01:12:59,678 --> 01:13:02,178
I only grabbed it lightly to stretch my shoulders.

1835
01:13:02,488 --> 01:13:03,917
- But it... - Just how strong are you?

1836
01:13:03,918 --> 01:13:06,117
No, it was loose.

1837
01:13:06,118 --> 01:13:07,588
- I mean... This is... - That's...

1838
01:13:07,658 --> 01:13:09,158
He's like the Hulk.

1839
01:13:16,068 --> 01:13:18,967
- It was a first for me too. - He's incredibly strong.

1840
01:13:18,968 --> 01:13:21,338
(Quickly fixing it)

1841
01:13:23,008 --> 01:13:26,908
(Dumbfounded)

1842
01:13:28,734 --> 01:13:31,103
(Did something happen?)

1843
01:13:31,104 --> 01:13:32,233
I reported it to the district office,

1844
01:13:32,234 --> 01:13:33,404
- Well done. - and they took care of it.

1845
01:13:35,374 --> 01:13:38,414
(He quickly flees the scene.)

1846
01:13:41,214 --> 01:13:43,914
(A subway station?)

1847
01:13:45,484 --> 01:13:48,884
(Where did he go after coming down to a subway station?)

1848
01:13:50,794 --> 01:13:53,164
(Striding effortlessly as he's familiar with the place)

1849
01:13:53,894 --> 01:13:55,424
It's the nation's beloved store.

1850
01:13:56,394 --> 01:13:59,504
I just stop by the store on purpose on the way home...

1851
01:14:00,004 --> 01:14:01,104
even though there's nothing I want to buy.

1852
01:14:01,364 --> 01:14:04,134
But I always end up with something in my hands when I leave.

1853
01:14:04,304 --> 01:14:05,434
You can never leave the store empty-handed.

1854
01:14:06,304 --> 01:14:08,374
I came to live in Seoul after retaking the CSAT.

1855
01:14:08,504 --> 01:14:10,714
It cost a lot to live alone in the city.

1856
01:14:10,974 --> 01:14:12,384
My parents paid my tuition,

1857
01:14:12,844 --> 01:14:15,854
so I tried to earn my own allowances.

1858
01:14:15,914 --> 01:14:18,084
I naturally developed a habit of being budget-conscious.

1859
01:14:18,314 --> 01:14:19,884
- That's true. - That's true.

1860
01:14:20,924 --> 01:14:24,794
Around 80 percent of household goods is from that store.

1861
01:14:26,394 --> 01:14:28,494
(Thinking)

1862
01:14:29,234 --> 01:14:32,294
(Staring intently)

1863
01:14:32,404 --> 01:14:34,264
It's 2 dollars for 6.

1864
01:14:35,334 --> 01:14:37,234
It's a good store for items like that.

1865
01:14:38,474 --> 01:14:41,004
One dollar for three. One dollar for four.

1866
01:14:42,004 --> 01:14:43,114
One dollar for four.

1867
01:14:43,774 --> 01:14:44,843
Then...

1868
01:14:44,844 --> 01:14:46,284
(He picked a set of 4 he could get at 1 dollar.)

1869
01:14:47,044 --> 01:14:50,284
(Super focused)

1870
01:14:50,984 --> 01:14:51,984
Seventy...

1871
01:14:51,985 --> 01:14:53,483
(It's 1 dollar for 70.)

1872
01:14:53,484 --> 01:14:55,554
(1 dollar for 50)

1873
01:14:57,424 --> 01:14:58,693
(He picked a set of 70 he could get at 1 dollar.)

1874
01:14:58,694 --> 01:15:01,794
All flosses are similar.

1875
01:15:01,864 --> 01:15:03,093
So I got one with a higher quantity.

1876
01:15:03,094 --> 01:15:04,134
(I see.)

1877
01:15:05,464 --> 01:15:09,403
(He compares each dish sponge.)

1878
01:15:09,404 --> 01:15:10,474
He's really careful.

1879
01:15:12,004 --> 01:15:14,804
(He picked one that costs 1 dollar.)

1880
01:15:15,344 --> 01:15:17,474
There are many excellent items that cost one dollar.

1881
01:15:17,544 --> 01:15:20,784
If it's above three dollars, it's no longer an option.

1882
01:15:21,414 --> 01:15:23,584
If it's 2 dollars, I'd wonder why it's 2 dollars.

1883
01:15:23,954 --> 01:15:26,854
I'd compare it to the one-dollar item similar to it.

1884
01:15:27,184 --> 01:15:30,554
If it's not worth spending twice as much, I'd get the one-dollar one.

1885
01:15:31,024 --> 01:15:33,194
I calculate fast. I'd compare them,

1886
01:15:33,494 --> 01:15:35,893
and if there's a reason it costs three dollars, then I'd get it.

1887
01:15:35,894 --> 01:15:37,834
Otherwise, I get the one-dollar item.

1888
01:15:37,934 --> 01:15:38,934
I can relate to that.

1889
01:15:38,934 --> 01:15:39,934
(Calculating the cost-effectiveness in his head)

1890
01:15:40,564 --> 01:15:45,274
(Looking around in search of cost-effective items)

1891
01:15:47,304 --> 01:15:48,304
What is it?

1892
01:15:50,044 --> 01:15:51,144
A decorating item.

1893
01:15:53,414 --> 01:15:57,784
(Evaluating cost-effectiveness)

1894
01:15:58,384 --> 01:16:01,124
(Grabbing)

1895
01:16:01,324 --> 01:16:02,894
You have a few of them at home.

1896
01:16:03,424 --> 01:16:04,854
- I have about two at home. - Right?

1897
01:16:05,554 --> 01:16:07,594
(A little treat while shopping on a budget)

1898
01:16:08,764 --> 01:16:11,934
Owls are considered symbols of wealth.

1899
01:16:13,634 --> 01:16:15,664
After I brought that home,

1900
01:16:16,074 --> 01:16:17,504
things started working out for me.

1901
01:16:19,974 --> 01:16:21,304
So I got another owl.

1902
01:16:21,904 --> 01:16:23,514
That's luxury to me.

1903
01:16:24,644 --> 01:16:29,553
(Holding the luxury owl tightly,)

1904
01:16:29,554 --> 01:16:32,184
(he heads to check out.)

1905
01:16:36,194 --> 01:16:37,323
(Happiness of 10.5 dollars including the luxury owl)

1906
01:16:37,324 --> 01:16:38,324
He grabbed a lot of items,

1907
01:16:38,325 --> 01:16:40,294
- but it only cost 10.5 dollars? - It's the best.

1908
01:16:41,024 --> 01:16:43,534
Happiness of 10 dollars in 2026?

1909
01:16:44,334 --> 01:16:47,334
(Putting them in his backpack 1 by 1)

1910
01:16:49,004 --> 01:16:52,374
(That was incredible shopping.)

1911
01:16:53,544 --> 01:16:55,704
(His steps are light as he shopped smart.)

1912
01:16:57,574 --> 01:16:58,774
Hello.

1913
01:16:59,444 --> 01:17:00,444
Welcome.

1914
01:17:00,445 --> 01:17:01,583
(Seon Min heads somewhere.)

1915
01:17:01,584 --> 01:17:02,654
A fruit store?

1916
01:17:02,884 --> 01:17:03,914
Is it a market?

1917
01:17:04,254 --> 01:17:06,084
It's a store I go to as often as Daiso.

1918
01:17:06,924 --> 01:17:08,483
(Fresh and...)

1919
01:17:08,484 --> 01:17:09,554
(cheap)

1920
01:17:10,294 --> 01:17:11,294
(Seon Min's favorite vegetable store)

1921
01:17:11,295 --> 01:17:12,924
- It's cheap. My goodness. - It's cheap.

1922
01:17:13,224 --> 01:17:15,764
Vegetables are much cheaper at a market like that.

1923
01:17:16,234 --> 01:17:17,894
I buy vegetables there, no matter what.

1924
01:17:19,304 --> 01:17:21,804
(Staring)

1925
01:17:23,004 --> 01:17:25,004
(Let's see.)

1926
01:17:28,104 --> 01:17:31,374
(Scanning carefully for plump garlic)

1927
01:17:32,114 --> 01:17:33,814
(He's done picking garlic.)

1928
01:17:36,284 --> 01:17:39,723
(On top of garlic and chili, he gets Karahyang mandarins too.)

1929
01:17:39,724 --> 01:17:40,984
I'll take these.

1930
01:17:42,654 --> 01:17:44,393
It's 7.5 dollars.

1931
01:17:44,394 --> 01:17:45,863
(Total: 7.5 dollars)

1932
01:17:45,864 --> 01:17:47,263
That's only 7.5 dollars?

1933
01:17:47,264 --> 01:17:48,294
That's cheap.

1934
01:17:49,564 --> 01:17:51,094
- Thank you. - Have a good day.

1935
01:17:52,664 --> 01:17:54,704
(Trudging after getting vegetables)

1936
01:17:57,134 --> 01:18:00,804
(He comes back home after a successful grocery run.)

1937
01:18:02,544 --> 01:18:05,514
(Exhausted)

1938
01:18:08,414 --> 01:18:10,514
(Putting away the vegetables as soon as he gets home)

1939
01:18:11,484 --> 01:18:13,284
(Piling 1 by 1)

1940
01:18:19,124 --> 01:18:22,294
(Gulping down)

1941
01:18:23,864 --> 01:18:24,964
(Dripping)

1942
01:18:25,234 --> 01:18:26,334
(Coughing)

1943
01:18:26,504 --> 01:18:27,634
(Coughing)

1944
01:18:28,004 --> 01:18:29,133
That happens.

1945
01:18:29,134 --> 01:18:30,803
(Choking up on water)

1946
01:18:30,804 --> 01:18:32,434
Why are you so impatient?

1947
01:18:32,874 --> 01:18:35,743
He has the energy of a dad when he's single.

1948
01:18:35,744 --> 01:18:36,814
- I know. - Yes.

1949
01:18:37,614 --> 01:18:39,544
(Coughing)

1950
01:18:40,314 --> 01:18:41,314
Goodness.

1951
01:18:43,314 --> 01:18:48,954
(Coughing again for the 2nd time)

1952
01:18:49,994 --> 01:18:53,324
(It's time to wash off the sweat.)

1953
01:18:56,364 --> 01:18:58,134
(Wiping)

1954
01:19:00,734 --> 01:19:03,404
(Pressing hard)

1955
01:19:04,134 --> 01:19:07,944
(The lotion he barely managed to squeeze out in the morning)

1956
01:19:08,804 --> 01:19:11,413
(He's struggling with lotion again.)

1957
01:19:11,414 --> 01:19:13,513
Will any of it come out?

1958
01:19:13,514 --> 01:19:15,184
(It looks like he'll squeeze out what's not even there.)

1959
01:19:16,984 --> 01:19:19,424
I feel like the plastic will melt out instead of the lotion.

1960
01:19:19,654 --> 01:19:20,754
(Grunting)

1961
01:19:21,424 --> 01:19:22,424
(Grunting)

1962
01:19:23,024 --> 01:19:25,323
(A tiny amount)

1963
01:19:25,324 --> 01:19:26,424
A bit of it came out.

1964
01:19:27,264 --> 01:19:29,734
(He uses even the last drop of it.)

1965
01:19:33,034 --> 01:19:35,764
(Opening)

1966
01:19:36,474 --> 01:19:40,204
(He washes the clothes he wore that day.)

1967
01:19:44,344 --> 01:19:46,684
(Where did it go?)

1968
01:19:48,444 --> 01:19:49,884
(Taking)

1969
01:19:52,254 --> 01:19:53,954
- Shampoo? - You use shampoo for it?

1970
01:19:54,354 --> 01:19:55,483
You use that?

1971
01:19:55,484 --> 01:19:57,824
I have a lot of leftover shampoo.

1972
01:19:57,924 --> 01:19:59,563
I have hair loss,

1973
01:19:59,564 --> 01:20:02,064
so I get a lot of hair loss shampoo as a gift.

1974
01:20:02,194 --> 01:20:04,464
But it's a waste to throw out the ones that expired.

1975
01:20:05,134 --> 01:20:07,264
So I use them as a detergent.

1976
01:20:07,534 --> 01:20:08,534
But...

1977
01:20:09,434 --> 01:20:11,074
Is it okay to use that?

1978
01:20:11,234 --> 01:20:13,504
I used it to wash clothes a lot in the military, though.

1979
01:20:13,904 --> 01:20:14,943
- Yes. - That's right.

1980
01:20:14,944 --> 01:20:16,773
- It's non-toxic. - It has strong cleansing power.

1981
01:20:16,774 --> 01:20:17,774
I see.

1982
01:20:17,775 --> 01:20:21,913
I feel like Seon Min is the perfect ambassador for Greenpeace.

1983
01:20:21,914 --> 01:20:24,283
- Greenpeace. - Greenpeace. He protects the Earth.

1984
01:20:24,284 --> 01:20:26,623
I do believe I should be mindful first.

1985
01:20:26,624 --> 01:20:27,723
- That's right. - Be mindful first?

1986
01:20:27,724 --> 01:20:28,783
- I have that belief. - You're the one...

1987
01:20:28,784 --> 01:20:30,223
- Of course. - who loves nature.

1988
01:20:30,224 --> 01:20:31,724
- "I should save things first." - Yes.

1989
01:20:35,024 --> 01:20:39,804
(He diligently folds the remaining laundry as well.)

1990
01:20:45,434 --> 01:20:48,273
(Opening the shelf...)

1991
01:20:48,274 --> 01:20:49,343
He's good at organizing.

1992
01:20:49,344 --> 01:20:51,113
(and putting the towels in)

1993
01:20:51,114 --> 01:20:52,444
- Good. - That makes me feel good.

1994
01:20:54,284 --> 01:20:58,284
(Putting away other clothes 1 by 1)

1995
01:21:00,524 --> 01:21:02,923
- He's good at basic organization. - Yes.

1996
01:21:02,924 --> 01:21:04,623
- I know. - He just has a lot of stuff.

1997
01:21:04,624 --> 01:21:06,393
- That's right. - He's well-organized.

1998
01:21:06,394 --> 01:21:07,564
Right, I am.

1999
01:21:08,824 --> 01:21:11,234
(All done.)

2000
01:21:12,834 --> 01:21:15,634
(Throwing)

2001
01:21:16,474 --> 01:21:18,404
(Goodness)

2002
01:21:19,234 --> 01:21:20,244
(Grunting)

2003
01:21:22,474 --> 01:21:23,574
He finally lay down.

2004
01:21:24,174 --> 01:21:25,544
- That must feel refreshing. - How nice.

2005
01:21:26,014 --> 01:21:27,144
That's when it's most relaxing.

2006
01:21:30,454 --> 01:21:32,584
(Dropping)

2007
01:21:33,624 --> 01:21:38,494
(Moving up and down)

2008
01:21:38,724 --> 01:21:40,164
- There's a magnet on his belly. - It's...

2009
01:21:40,724 --> 01:21:43,164
Are you charging the phone wirelessly?

2010
01:21:44,134 --> 01:21:45,333
Charging wirelessly?

2011
01:21:45,334 --> 01:21:46,664
There's a magnet on his belly.

2012
01:21:48,634 --> 01:21:49,673
He's taking a nap.

2013
01:21:49,674 --> 01:21:50,804
(Charging the phone with his belly)

2014
01:21:51,434 --> 01:21:53,043
That's when napping feels the best.

2015
01:21:53,044 --> 01:21:54,904
- Right. You feel drowsy. - You can sleep soundly.

2016
01:21:56,344 --> 01:21:59,444
(I should get up, though.)

2017
01:22:01,444 --> 01:22:05,384
(Heading to the kitchen, resisting the temptation to take a nap)

2018
01:22:07,484 --> 01:22:08,753
It's time for lunch.

2019
01:22:08,754 --> 01:22:10,094
(He's so busy.)

2020
01:22:10,694 --> 01:22:12,524
(Rustling)

2021
01:22:13,724 --> 01:22:17,164
(He took out a whole chicken from the fridge?)

2022
01:22:18,064 --> 01:22:19,864
(Taking it out)

2023
01:22:20,364 --> 01:22:22,104
It's a dish I make often.

2024
01:22:22,304 --> 01:22:23,574
(What is it?)

2025
01:22:24,804 --> 01:22:28,344
(Putting it in cold water first)

2026
01:22:29,304 --> 01:22:31,814
(Tapping in)

2027
01:22:32,984 --> 01:22:34,214
- Is it one-pot chicken? - What is it?

2028
01:22:37,384 --> 01:22:39,183
(A bag of garlic he tore open on the side)

2029
01:22:39,184 --> 01:22:40,184
Garlic.

2030
01:22:40,584 --> 01:22:42,824
Washing them in the bag? Nice.

2031
01:22:43,354 --> 01:22:44,553
- That's smart. - I do that too.

2032
01:22:44,554 --> 01:22:46,494
- That way, you use less water. - That's right.

2033
01:22:47,894 --> 01:22:49,734
(Dripping)

2034
01:22:51,034 --> 01:22:52,333
He poured them out. Is he adding them all?

2035
01:22:52,334 --> 01:22:53,534
- Will he add them all? - He must be.

2036
01:22:55,034 --> 01:22:58,134
It's the food I eat when I'm low on energy.

2037
01:22:58,474 --> 01:23:00,574
"All this garlic will go into my stomach."

2038
01:23:01,004 --> 01:23:02,473
It's ginseng chicken soup loaded with garlic.

2039
01:23:02,474 --> 01:23:03,573
(Seon Min's special dish)

2040
01:23:03,574 --> 01:23:04,914
Yes, you must have ginseng chicken soup.

2041
01:23:05,114 --> 01:23:09,284
(The soup starts to boil.)

2042
01:23:11,554 --> 01:23:15,484
(Since it's been boiled, he turns off the gas.)

2043
01:23:16,754 --> 01:23:18,124
There are impurities.

2044
01:23:18,794 --> 01:23:20,464
- I boil it once to filter them. - That's right.

2045
01:23:20,724 --> 01:23:22,264
(Amazed)

2046
01:23:24,134 --> 01:23:26,864
(A bag of herbal medicine that'll boost his energy)

2047
01:23:28,004 --> 01:23:31,074
(Adding lots of garlic, which is Seon Min's favorite)

2048
01:23:31,804 --> 01:23:33,503
It's somewhat relaxing.

2049
01:23:33,504 --> 01:23:34,804
(As he's skilled)

2050
01:23:35,974 --> 01:23:39,544
(Putting them deep into the hot water)

2051
01:23:40,214 --> 01:23:43,114
(Okay, it's all done.)

2052
01:23:43,814 --> 01:23:46,283
Watching him cook gives me the courage to try myself.

2053
01:23:46,284 --> 01:23:47,454
That's right.

2054
01:23:48,054 --> 01:23:49,253
Come over. I'll cook for you.

2055
01:23:49,254 --> 01:23:50,254
- Really? - Really?

2056
01:23:50,255 --> 01:23:53,093
I'll bring over spring water from the mountain nearby house.

2057
01:23:53,094 --> 01:23:54,223
- That'd be really nice. - It's better...

2058
01:23:54,224 --> 01:23:55,393
if you cook with spring water.

2059
01:23:55,394 --> 01:23:56,764
(Yes! I'll make sure to go over to your place.)

2060
01:23:59,194 --> 01:24:00,234
Okay.

2061
01:24:02,434 --> 01:24:05,604
(Wrapping it up with pepper)

2062
01:24:08,404 --> 01:24:09,444
Okay.

2063
01:24:09,874 --> 01:24:11,243
Please be cooked fast.

2064
01:24:11,244 --> 01:24:12,844
(He just needs to boil it now.)

2065
01:24:17,714 --> 01:24:19,314
I don't think I'm lonely.

2066
01:24:21,024 --> 01:24:25,254
Surprisingly, this house is like paradise for me.

2067
01:24:26,054 --> 01:24:29,394
I'm taking this house as a foundation to work hard,

2068
01:24:29,694 --> 01:24:30,963
take good care of my health,

2069
01:24:30,964 --> 01:24:33,104
and give a reward to my body from time to time.

2070
01:24:33,734 --> 01:24:35,104
By collecting good energy,

2071
01:24:35,604 --> 01:24:37,833
I want to become a comedian who gives great laughs.

2072
01:24:37,834 --> 01:24:39,074
That's my goal.

2073
01:24:40,874 --> 01:24:42,274
(Blowing)

2074
01:24:45,244 --> 01:24:48,144
(Amazed)

2075
01:24:49,044 --> 01:24:50,713
- Bravo! - The scent of garlic...

2076
01:24:50,714 --> 01:24:51,784
and herbal medicine.

2077
01:24:52,284 --> 01:24:53,524
That's all you need.

2078
01:24:53,654 --> 01:24:58,294
(A perfect day that relieved built-up fatigue)

2079
01:25:01,994 --> 01:25:05,993
(Seon Min is Almost Unstoppable)

2080
01:25:05,994 --> 01:25:07,934
- Thank you for the clip. - Thank you.

2081
01:25:08,764 --> 01:25:11,273
- I was really happy watching it. - I was happy.

2082
01:25:11,274 --> 01:25:12,334
- Right. - Yes.

2083
01:25:12,574 --> 01:25:16,714
He's one of the comedians I almost always watch before I sleep.

2084
01:25:18,074 --> 01:25:20,243
I leave his video on because I like the lively energy...

2085
01:25:20,244 --> 01:25:21,613
he gives off.

2086
01:25:21,614 --> 01:25:24,484
And I'm not very active at home.

2087
01:25:25,184 --> 01:25:27,923
I want to try the food he makes.

2088
01:25:27,924 --> 01:25:29,693
(He wants to try the food Seon Min makes.)

2089
01:25:29,694 --> 01:25:32,693
He's the most solid among the people of my age...

2090
01:25:32,694 --> 01:25:34,964
that I know of.

2091
01:25:35,794 --> 01:25:36,934
- Thank you. - I'm happy.

2092
01:25:37,134 --> 01:25:38,533
Watching you made us happy...

2093
01:25:38,534 --> 01:25:39,593
even though you didn't do anything special.

2094
01:25:39,594 --> 01:25:43,404
Now I know why Seon Min is so widely loved.

2095
01:25:43,774 --> 01:25:45,134
He's the real deal.

2096
01:25:45,404 --> 01:25:47,343
- He doesn't exaggerate. - Right, he doesn't!

2097
01:25:47,344 --> 01:25:48,403
His daily life we saw today...

2098
01:25:48,404 --> 01:25:49,444
- wasn't exaggerated too. - That's right.

2099
01:25:49,544 --> 01:25:52,043
I think that's his charm.

2100
01:25:52,044 --> 01:25:54,383
I hope we get to see you often.

2101
01:25:54,384 --> 01:25:56,213
- Please come again. - I hope so too. Thank you.

2102
01:25:56,214 --> 01:25:57,513
- Thank you! - Thank you!

2103
01:25:57,514 --> 01:25:58,683
(We root for Seon Min's future endeavors.)

2104
01:25:58,684 --> 01:26:00,254
(Next story)

2105
01:26:01,184 --> 01:26:02,923
(The cute scene-stealer from "Undercover Miss Hong...")

2106
01:26:02,924 --> 01:26:04,294
(that drew everyone's attention)

2107
01:26:05,354 --> 01:26:06,964
(She was even nominated at the Baeksang Arts Awards.)

2108
01:26:07,324 --> 01:26:09,834
(The rookie actor who burst onto the scene)

2109
01:26:10,294 --> 01:26:12,363
(It's been 3 years since she started living alone.)

2110
01:26:12,364 --> 01:26:14,464
(Actress Choi Ji Su)

2111
01:26:15,504 --> 01:26:16,933
(Her small and precious roommate)

2112
01:26:16,934 --> 01:26:18,434
(Gamja)

2113
01:26:19,034 --> 01:26:22,344
(Welcome to Ji Su's house where Gamja lives too.)

2114
01:26:22,904 --> 01:26:25,774
(You can tell how skilled she is from every corner of her house.)

2115
01:26:26,484 --> 01:26:28,914
(She keeps her stuff thoroughly.)

2116
01:26:29,584 --> 01:26:33,084
(Solemnly with gloves on)

2117
01:26:33,784 --> 01:26:37,254
(A ritual she has to do every week)

2118
01:26:38,094 --> 01:26:40,524
(Cleaning like crazy)

2119
01:26:40,924 --> 01:26:42,523
(Cleaning...)

2120
01:26:42,524 --> 01:26:43,964
(gives her a dopamine boost.)

2121
01:26:44,464 --> 01:26:48,004
(Bathrooms show how you live.)

2122
01:26:48,364 --> 01:26:49,633
(Since it's my life, I'll clean every nook and cranny...)

2123
01:26:49,634 --> 01:26:50,704
(so it shines.)

2124
01:26:51,034 --> 01:26:53,244
(Shining)

2125
01:26:54,274 --> 01:26:57,574
(She becomes happier if she cleans this hard.)

2126
01:26:58,274 --> 01:27:01,314
(The dopamine boost party does not stop.)

2127
01:27:01,914 --> 01:27:02,914
(Switching...)

2128
01:27:02,915 --> 01:27:04,814
(the tools)

2129
01:27:05,314 --> 01:27:08,024
(Getting a full dopamine boost after switching the tools)

2130
01:27:08,424 --> 01:27:10,153
(She even explodes...)

2131
01:27:10,154 --> 01:27:11,694
(with cleaning the washing machine.)

2132
01:27:12,154 --> 01:27:13,664
(It's thrilling.)

2133
01:27:14,424 --> 01:27:17,034
(I Cleaned Thoroughly Again Today)

2134
01:27:17,934 --> 01:27:20,834
(Here's another man who is cleaning his house.)

2135
01:27:21,304 --> 01:27:22,304
All right.

2136
01:27:22,305 --> 01:27:24,033
(A refreshing day...)

2137
01:27:24,034 --> 01:27:25,374
(for a new beginning)

2138
01:27:25,804 --> 01:27:27,473
(His new family,)

2139
01:27:27,474 --> 01:27:29,003
(a new mattress)

2140
01:27:29,004 --> 01:27:30,373
- I don't think it'll work. - No?

2141
01:27:30,374 --> 01:27:32,014
(No?)

2142
01:27:32,474 --> 01:27:34,143
(Feeling especially upset today for having no elevator)

2143
01:27:34,144 --> 01:27:35,744
(I'm sorry about this.)

2144
01:27:35,944 --> 01:27:37,213
(You can just push it.)

2145
01:27:37,214 --> 01:27:39,354
(I'm pushing.)

2146
01:27:41,084 --> 01:27:42,984
(Struggling)

2147
01:27:43,154 --> 01:27:44,154
(Ringing)

2148
01:27:44,724 --> 01:27:46,564
(No! I didn't mean to press the doorbell.)

2149
01:27:48,194 --> 01:27:49,264
(Oh, no. It came off.)

2150
01:27:49,664 --> 01:27:51,334
(Am I dreaming?)

2151
01:27:51,794 --> 01:27:54,104
(Soaked in sweat)

2152
01:27:55,064 --> 01:27:57,274
(I must see it through. I'll freshen up the balcony too.)

2153
01:27:57,634 --> 01:27:59,704
(Putting on the scrubber)

2154
01:28:00,604 --> 01:28:02,144
(Splashing)

2155
01:28:02,674 --> 01:28:04,544
(Oh, my. This feels so clean.)

2156
01:28:04,944 --> 01:28:06,814
(Goodbye, deep-seated grime!)

2157
01:28:11,584 --> 01:28:14,984
(Refresh Day)
